{"units": [{"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ of the ⟦2⟧, which comes fresh from the ⟦3⟧ (cf. ⟦4⟧, Ddf., and ⟦5⟧ Frg. 321). Wecklein wants ⟦6⟧, like ⟦7⟧ ⟦8⟧, because / - - (word unity in the measure of the ionic a minore), in the 4th and 5th feet does not occur in A.; see, however, (Dindorf Po. Scaen. Praef. 34) ⟦9⟧ ⟦10⟧. ⟦11⟧(⟦12⟧) 577. 641. ⟦13⟧. ⟦14⟧ 1013. There is also no example in A. where ⟦15⟧- is certainly monosyllabic (cf. on 513), except ⟦16⟧ Frg. 510. The rite is again described by Apollonius IV, 702 ff.: (Circe) ⟦17⟧, ⟦18⟧, ⟦19⟧, ⟦20⟧· ⟦21⟧, ⟦22⟧, etc. Cf. above on 280ff., also on the fact that according to Orestes' opinion the purification is strengthened by subsequent intercourse on journeys and in houses, V. 451 f., where ⟦23⟧ must be written for ⟦24⟧ (which is certainly assimilated after 450). Cf. 240 ⟦25⟧. ⟦26⟧ ⟦27⟧. The asyndetic beginning 451 stands for ⟦28⟧, with emphatic preposing of ⟦29⟧. But striking is ⟦30⟧ instead of ⟦31⟧ (Ddf.): Orestes has not become ⟦32⟧, but only ⟦33⟧, and also ⟦34⟧ (the blood-guilt) can fittingly be object only to ⟦35⟧. I would therefore also write ⟦36⟧; elsewhere neither this nor that verb is found in the tragedians. 453"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned1", "translation": "of a newly born animal"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned2", "translation": "piglet"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned3", "translation": "teat"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned4", "translation": "with good teats"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned5", "translation": "a piglet with good teats"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned6", "translation": "newly born"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned7", "translation": "the might of Polyphontes"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned8", "translation": "the might of Polyneices"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned9", "translation": "n"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned10", "translation": "Polyn"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned11", "translation": "corpse"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned12", "translation": "neo"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned13", "translation": "chick"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned14", "translation": "first, a release from unyielding bloodshed, stretching over her the offspring of a sow"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned15", "translation": "whose teats still swelled from the womb of birth"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned16", "translation": "she wet her hands with blood"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned17", "translation": "cutting the throat"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned18", "translation": "and again she appeased with other libations"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned19", "translation": "calling upon Zeus the purifier"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned20", "translation": "to those who go"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned21", "translation": "to cattle"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned22", "translation": "crossing alike land and sea"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned23", "translation": "from the sea of Rhytas"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned24", "translation": "but we long ago"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned25", "translation": "long ago"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned26", "translation": "let us consecrate"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned27", "translation": "let us purify"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned28", "translation": "sacred"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned29", "translation": "holy"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned30", "translation": "these things"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned31", "translation": "to purify oneself"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-mentioned32", "translation": "let us purify"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-179-1-quote1", "translation": "freshly plucked"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-180-1-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧: namely ⟦2⟧;"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-180-1-mentioned1", "translation": "out of the way"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-180-1-mentioned2", "translation": "to be"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-181-1-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ = ⟦2⟧ as at 432."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-181-1-mentioned1", "translation": "I say"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-181-1-mentioned2", "translation": "I command"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-182-1-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ at the end of the verse also at 419."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-182-1-mentioned1", "translation": "you will learn soon"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-182-2-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ 455 = ⟦2⟧, ⟦3⟧."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-182-2-mentioned1", "translation": "you inquire"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-182-2-mentioned2", "translation": "you know"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-182-3-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ only here, = -⟦2⟧ -⟦3⟧, which likewise does not occur in the tragedians. On 457 the scholiast correctly says: ⟦4⟧; cf. on 397 ff. The pleonasm in ⟦5⟧ we remove with ⟦6⟧ (adjectivally Wieseler, Headlam; on ⟦7⟧); for ⟦8⟧ one compares ⟦9⟧ ⟦10⟧, ⟦11⟧ 1545 cf. ⟦12⟧. ⟦13⟧, etc."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-182-3-mentioned1", "translation": "Harmostor"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-182-3-mentioned2", "translation": "ster"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-182-3-mentioned3", "translation": "stes"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-182-3-mentioned4", "translation": "through these things he makes the goddess friendly"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-182-3-mentioned5", "translation": "Troy"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-182-3-mentioned6", "translation": "Trojan"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-182-3-mentioned7", "translation": "a city without a city"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-182-3-mentioned8", "translation": "a lawless law"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-182-3-mentioned9", "translation": "a graceless grace"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-182-4-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ (only here) refers to the dark, cruel disposition, cf. ⟦2⟧ and ⟦3⟧ Ag. 462. 1511, ⟦4⟧ (Solon) 42 Bgk. The epic (⟦5⟧)⟦6⟧ the tragedians seem (against Homer) to measure with ā, Kühner-Blaſs II, 468."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-182-4-mentioned1", "translation": "dark-minded"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-182-4-mentioned2", "translation": "dark Erinyes"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-182-4-mentioned3", "translation": "black Ares"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-182-4-mentioned4", "translation": "from a black heart"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-182-4-mentioned5", "translation": "kat"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-182-4-mentioned6", "translation": "ekta"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-182-5-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ like ⟦2⟧ of the same garment ⟦3⟧;"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-182-5-mentioned1", "translation": "with embroidered"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-182-5-mentioned2", "translation": "of the embroidery"}]}